WEBVTT

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.920
Give alien weapons to Earth!

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.860
Give them to Earth!

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.250
The cries to repel alien forces and

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.610
strengthen Earth defenses 
have been intensifying.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.640
That would lead to the 
path of destruction.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.810
Until now, the masses have

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.910
considered this war 
someone else's problem.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.770
We will mass produce AHSMB units 
on the Rhinos' production line.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.080
Is that why you disclosed information 
regarding the Rhinos units?

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:04.950
"Deep Recon"

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.840
Dang! So, would defeating 
a Lega-whatever in a game

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.710
be like vanquishing a midboss?

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.210
Wasn't he a "Legatus"?

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:09.650
It's their Military 
Commander equivalent.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.940
Is a Military Commander high ranking?

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:12.860
Shouldn't he be?

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.340
Then isn't it about time we shed 
our title as the Fail Five?

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:18.860
Not if each midboss 
trashes all of our units.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:21.760
Repairs are only 28% done for mine...

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.780
Mine is in similar shape.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.770
You two have it good!

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.900
They said mine's smashed 
like a water flea.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.380
What's a "water flea"?

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.040
A crustacean of the Branchiopoda class,

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.170
Diplostraca order, Cladocera suborder,

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.460
Anomopoda suborder, Daphniidae 
family, Daphnia genus.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.220
In layman's terms, it's 
a type of plankton.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.660
Oh, okay! But what does that 
have to do with your AHSMB?

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.550
Beats me.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:43.970
Didn't you pay attention?!

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.760
Anyway, doesn't vanquishing 
a midboss unlock

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.270
an event that leads to power ups?

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.350
No, heroes are supposed to train next!

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.170
I don't wanna train.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:55.320
Here! Thanks for waiting for Meal Set A.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.720
Asagi, I gave you an extra serving.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.400
I can't eat all of this.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:00.630
Then I'll he-

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.010
You can have half of mine.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.570
Nah, I'll pass...

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:04.720
What's wrong?

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.050
I'm not feeling terribly hungry.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:08.500
That's not cool!

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:11.710
A hero must always eat well 
and sleep well, remember?

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.630
Randy! And Officer Ange, too.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:16.820
Yep! Mr. Cool is in the house!

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.570
I heard you had a rough fight.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.380
I know how to perk ya back up.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.450
Why do we have to watch 
this in my room?!

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.690
Like it matters!

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:28.810
So whadda ya think of this one?

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.620
Where are you going?!

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.310
M-man, I've only got eyes for guns...

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.960
You won't know until you try.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.020
He's right!

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.690
Isn't it nice how girls 
are so cute and soft?

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:37.650
I like 'em firm!

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.440
I don't see it. You must 
have rather unusual taste.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:44.260
Say, doesn't this actress 
kinda resemble Captain Amane?

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.580
You really have a thing for your 
superior officers, don't you?

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.310
Randy is definitely the type 
that loves to get stepped on!

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.250
Is that what turns you on, Randy?

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:56.730
Yeah! Aren't the kinda strict 
"big sister" types awesome?

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.860
I quiver with delight each 
time they order me around.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:03:59.920
Masochistic freak.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:03.780
Officer... Ange?! How 
long have you been here?

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:04.780
From the start.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:05.700
Crap!

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.870
What the hell?! Why'd you turn it off?

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.620
Why is he in Violent Mode?

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:10.750
Listen up!

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.650
Nothing pisses me off more 
than when someone kills

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:14.260
a video when I'm watching it.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.020
You'd better remember that!

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.980
Doesn't watching this give 
you the same sense of elation

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.490
as when we're fighting?

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.970
That's because the content 
is meant to arouse you.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.510
That's not what I meant.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.680
The realization that I'm alive

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.670
gushes up from the bottom of my heart.

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:29.830
It's like someone is 
telling me that I must

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.660
defeat more foes and survive!

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:35.060
That is precisely why 
I watch these videos.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:38.150
When I watch them, I feel 
as though I am truly alive.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:42.740
By experiencing the ritual related to 
the creation and birth of new life,

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:45.490
my resolve to fight to protect 
the next generation...

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:47.850
Uh, what was I gonna say?

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.060
You were trying to 
sound cool and failed!

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.350
No surprise coming from 
a failure at life.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.760
Who'd you call a "failure"?!

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.250
That's your nickname!

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.650
I'm a "bummer"!

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:00.110
I can't hear a thing! 
I can't see a thing!

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.440
Don't call yourself that!

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.200
I-I know!

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:03.490
Guys, what do you plan on 
doing once the war is over?

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.860
To be honest, there is 
something I'd like to do.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.890
Huh? Did I say something wrong?

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.290
Nah, not really.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.880
Just wonderin', is Patrick an airhead?

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:15.890
That's right.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.580
Then I shouldn't hold it against him.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:24.190
Oh, yeah! I ordered a new video, 
so you can have this one.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.700
Thank you very much!

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.370
Don't wind up makin' that girl 
cry with all these videos!

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.530
Who is "that girl"?

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.510
Meh, forget it.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.950
This? I have a fiancée back on Earth.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.120
A fiancée?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.670
Yeah. My parents picked her 
out back when I was a kid.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:44.090
But when I met her, she 
was just so cute and kind!

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.720
She's also very kind hearted, 
domestic and understanding!

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.560
I fell in love at first sight.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:52.450
Aren't you getting married 
when the war is over?

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.370
Y-yeah.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:56.630
You're getting married? Congratulations!

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:58.810
We've gotta work hard so that you can!

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:00.830
Do you have a hologram of her?

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.290
Sure do! Wanna see?

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:04.940
Well? Isn't she cute?

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:06.720
She really is cute!

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:08.370
I know, right?

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:10.370
That's cute?

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.420
She his mom?

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:15.450
The 1st and 2nd Mobile Units' 
supplies are down to 30%.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.830
Their warships are burning 
through artillery.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:21.040
It hurts to have lost all of 
those skilled pilots, doesn't it?

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:24.820
Indeed. We can always build new 
fighters, but not new pilots...

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.970
Even if you combined the Bela-Russian 
and Great Chinese Alliance's forces

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.820
with the Organization 
of American States,

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:31.830
Europe Union and Pacific 
Rim-India Alliance,

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.680
we would not survive a

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.870
full-scale invasion the next 
time Earth is attacked.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.500
In which case, the only 
thing we have in our favor

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.900
is the enemy's poor stamina.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.610
OPEN

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.460
Couldn't you manage somethin'?

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:43.480
Yakitori     Beer     Simmered Giblets

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:46.930
Those bunnies put up a pretty 
good fight in their AHSMBs.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:51.370
Their units were destroyed during 
the Gurantseere Defensive Battle.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:54.120
Man, and they were my only hope!

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.640
No wonder Reika was bent outta shape.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:59.310
I'm outta gas! I'm gonna 
die if I don't drink!

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.230
Then we oughta drink on her behalf.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.270
Yep! Keep it comin'!

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:10.680
None of the countries have any military 
might left and they're run by morons!

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.030
I'm up a river without a paddle!

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.390
Same here.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.850
I've got a secretive boss 
who's running me ragged

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:17.330
with preparing to launch the new 
mass production AHSMB models.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.480
Gimme!

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:19.370
This?

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:25.120
That, too. But gimme those AHSMBs.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:26.710
Sure, you can have 'em.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.420
Yay! You can't take that back later.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:33.340
That's nothing if it'll make 
life easier on those kids.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:40.410
A counter-attack combining 
all of Earth's forces, huh?

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.430
Those kids will lead the vanguard.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.270
We really are horrible, aren't we?
We really are horrible, aren't we?

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:52.860
The line extends beyond Uranus' 
orbit and in toward Jupiter...

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:55.490
So this is the Wulgaru's 
navigation route.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.390
You wish to destroy the gate?

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:00.330
Is that even possible?

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.560
I suppose...

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.980
If you destroyed the gate's controls,

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.190
within a certain period of 
time, the gate would close.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.850
Once it did, what would happen 
to the Wulgaru's invading army?

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.230
If they were cut from 
their supply route,

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:15.400
I imagine they would perish before long.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.200
Would they withdraw before that happens?

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.010
Knowing my brother...

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.910
We have secured enough to sustain you.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:24.600
I trust you.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.380
I love your planet, Earth.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:30.420
However, your star of hope 
is starting to grow clouded.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:32.330
Are you referring to Izuru Hitachi?

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.890
If you lose his protection,

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:38.310
your planet will probably 
fall into my brother's hands.

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.700
After he claims your genes, 
there will be nothing left.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:45.150
The Wulgaru truly are interested 
in nothing but our genes.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:49.570
For the Wulgaru, obtaining 
them is life's greatest joy.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:53.630
Do you know where the gate is located?

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:57.280
Even I do not know the 
current state of the gate.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:01.580
In order to locate the enemy's gate,

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:04.420
I need you to conduct a long-range 
tactical reconnaissance mission.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:06.520
What's this about a "gate"?

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:08.860
The gate is a dimensional 
hole that can be

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:10.810
created in locations with 
gravitic fluctuations.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.190
We believe the Wulgaru 
forced the gate open,

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:14.950
which is how they came 
to our solar system.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:16.220
You've heard this before!

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.110
I forgot.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:20.390
The chance of a safe 
return is extremely slim.

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:21.850
This is a perilous mission.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.040
You are the only ones 
capable of pulling it off.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.640
Wow, that's awesome!

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.210
Where is the gate?

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:30.940
It's past Saturn?!

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:34.830
Absurd! Humanity hasn't 
even reached Saturn yet.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.270
So it's a one-way ticket, eh?

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:37.220
Look at this.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.560
That's huge! It looks 
just like an erected-

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.120
What is that?

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:46.020
It's a booster bound to 
sublight-speed guided missiles.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:48.120
But it still won't be fast enough.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.170
We've also attached laser sails.

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:51.460
The laser propulsion will provide your

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:53.150
primary acceleration until 
you reach escape velocity.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.630
Is this even possible?

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:57.890
Theoretically, you can accelerate 
to 10% the speed of light.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.910
In which case, we'd reach 
our target in 50 hours.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.310
It will take 120 hours to 
reach maximum acceleration.

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:05.480
What's wrong?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.330
Wow, that startled me!

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:11.000
Venturing uncharted space!
 This is every man's dream!

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.230
Question, Ma'am!

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:15.050
Couldn't we take the Godinion?

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.650
The Godinion is too large 
to handle accelerating

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.910
on that makeshift booster.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:21.440
What if you forced it to?

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:23.720
I'm confident it would get torn apart.

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:26.250
Then what about our units?

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.460
According to my calculations, 
the Rhinos should be fine.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:29.900
According to your calculations...?

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.090
Is there a possibility that 
the enemy will find us?

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.390
You'll be fine getting there.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.320
But when returning, you'll 
decelerate upon making

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.900
a gravity turn at Jupiter.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.910
There is a possibility that 
they could strike then.

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:41.820
That's right.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:45.540
Let me reiterate: This mission must 
be carried out in absolute secrecy.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:49.430
Do not let the Wulgaru catch 
you searching for their gate.

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:52.980
The future of Earth rests on 
this reconnaissance mission!

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:54.800
We're counting on you.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:56.770
Yes, sir!

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:00.560
Commence Operation: Eagle Landed.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:04.650
Awesome! I've never seen a 
booster like that before.

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:06.660
We're doing a test run for 
a new top-secret weapon.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:08.460
Whatcha think? Pretty cool, right?

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.830
It's incredible!

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:12.590
Damn! I wish my unit 
wasn't all busted up.

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:15.150
There is no need for you to help.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.260
We can handle this one ourselves!

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:17.690
But-

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:20.470
Give us a chance to show 
off every now and then.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:23.530
Dude, I'll prove to ya that we're 
the real heroes around here.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.950
No, I'm not handing over 
my role as the hero.

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:29.810
Then let's duke it out to see who 
the real hero is when I get back.

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:31.230
I'm holding you to that.

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:33.270
Have I ever broken a promise?

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:35.190
You break them all of the time!

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.320
Yeah. It's far rarer 
for you to keep them.

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:39.880
Dudes, as my teammates, 
you oughta back me up!

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:44.870
Tamaki!

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.510
I'd like to tell you 
something when I get back.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.150
You would?

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:51.680
Want me to introduce you to Guiliano?

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:52.630
No, that's not it...

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:54.670
It's not? Then were you after Siegfried?

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:55.710
You've got it wrong!

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:57.920
Then was it Master Daneel all along?!

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.670
Whatever shall I do?

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:23.530
You haven't eaten since before 
that last mission, have you?

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:25.320
I could bake you a cake.

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.370
Cut the guy some slack.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:27.300
What was that?

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:51.540
Everyone!

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:53.810
It's time for your checkups.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:54.370
Checkups?

00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:57.310
Right. You just finished 
another big mission,

00:12:57.310 --> 00:12:59.130
so we're going to give you checkups.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:06.330
So? How'd it go, Patrick?

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:07.490
How'd what go?

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:08.710
Don't be so shy!

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.720
Didn't you tell Tamaki how 
you feel before we left?

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.370
N-n-n-not yet!

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:13.100
That's no fun.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:16.910
But I just found out what 
Tamaki's favorite food is.

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:18.040
I'll win her over with that.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:19.520
Oh, good thinking!

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.130
Are you seriously going to be okay?

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:24.100
I had some sent up all 
of the way from Earth.

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:25.660
I'll give it to her when I get back.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:26.800
Best of luck to ya!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:27.280
Thanks!

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.560
Tamaki Irie, please accept this.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:36.920
Tamaki Irie, please accept this.

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.450
I gained more weight!

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:48.160
I knew it!

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:50.490
They seem to be havin' fun over there...

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:51.720
It's grimy over here.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:53.790
It's stuffy and crowded!

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:03.380
Visual on Neptune.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:05.000
We've reached the final veering point.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.220
Wow! So that's Neptune!

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:10.020
We're the first humans in 
history to make it this far.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:12.860
I'm going to set our swing-by maneuver.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:13.890
I'm countin' on ya!

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:16.290
Which will it be: Heavy 
G and get there quick

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.330
or a slow and easy ride?

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:19.500
I'd prefer the easy-

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.440
Obviously we're gonna 
take the quicker method!

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:22.900
Yeah, I figured as much.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:23.670
Man!

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:26.320
Great! Report in via our secure line.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:27.070
Roger!

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:28.780
Static...?

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:29.670
What's wrong?

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:31.260
I can't get through.

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:33.740
Just a sec. I'll look into it.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:35.600
Problem found!

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.560
A solar storm is emitting

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:40.360
extremely strong electromagnetic 
interference.

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:41.650
What range are we lookin' at?

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.110
Everywhere between us... and Jupiter.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.500
Well, jeez! It looks like we're stuck

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.740
goin' home so we can hand the info over!

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:53.740
And here I thought this was an easy job

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.980
where we just transmitted 
the data we found.

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:58.410
Well, there's no such 
thing as an easy job!

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:03.730
Changing course.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.520
Disconnecting from the sails in

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:10.190
5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:11.180
Disconnect.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:17.410
We successfully disconnected.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.100
Sweet! Ignite the booster!

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:27.900
Even with a G canceler, this is brutal!

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.070
They oughta pay us overtime for this!

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:31.890
It would help cover all 
of my upcoming dates!

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:33.740
Just how much are you 
gonna spend on her?

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:37.520
We're gonna zoom by!

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:40.020
Set all of your sensors to 
auto. We can't miss the gate!

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:42.750
I see it!

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:48.900
Another exam?

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.660
Right. I'm concerned about some 
of the results that came up.

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:52.590
How is everyone else?

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:57.430
They will reach the rendezvous 
point in 10 hours.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:00.750
Due to a solar storm, we 
are unable to reach them.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:02.230
Can you find them via optical tracking?

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:03.810
It hasn't picked them up yet.

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:06.250
Do you think they're all right?

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:07.980
All we can do is go in 
the hopes that they are.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.540
Rate of deceleration 
increasing from 60 to 70.

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:14.010
We will reach our target 
speed in 30 seconds.

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:16.030
Be sure to keep your eyes peeled!

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.330
I'm pulling my radar up.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:19.850
We're under attack!

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:23.900
Patrick, can you get through?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.680
The solar storm is still interfering!

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:29.000
I see... Leave this to 
me and get outta here!

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:30.190
But-

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:31.860
Hurry! Every second counts!

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:32.840
Roger!

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:37.280
There is an emergency transmission!

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:40.660
Requesting reinforcements! Randy 
is currently engaging the-

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:43.600
Right now, we are at Jupi-

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:44.580
Did you get the data?

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:47.360
We can't receive it due to the strong 
interference from the solar storm!

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:50.050
No matter what the cost, 
you must recover that data!

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:51.090
Commander!

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:54.030
I repeat, retrieving that 
data takes top priority.

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:56.010
Roger.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:59.320
Siegfried, open the solar sails!

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:03.690
Guiliano, ask Star Rose for an 
emergency laser propulsion shot.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:04.460
Roger!

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:29.730
Do you think Randy will be all right?

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.760
We have to carry on his will.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.650
We must- we must- get 
this information back.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:41.060
It's the same fighter from earlier!

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:42.320
I'll hold him back!

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:43.060
Go, Patrick!

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:44.100
But-!

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:47.810
The fate of Earth rests 
on this information! Go!

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:48.790
Okay!

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.500
At the very least, I 
want you to survive.

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:13.400
First I'll take your right arm!

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:18.340
Then your left arm!

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:21.560
And your legs.

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:25.140
That was far too easy...

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:26.650
It was hardly beautiful.

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.130
I've gotta hurry and inform everyone!

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:38.680
Tamaki!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:53.670
Patrick!

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:57.190
My radar is... not malfunctioning.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.200
And my sensors are operational, too.

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:03.450
For him to have disappeared 
before anyone retrieved him...

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:04.410
Damn it!

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:07.660
I have to get back somehow...

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:11.040
If I don't relay this information, 
we really will have died like dogs!

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:23.050
I'm so close! Move, dammit!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:26.370
Is this the end?

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:27.980
Tally-ho!

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:31.310
Randy?! You're still alive?

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:33.730
Don't go killin' me off just yet!

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:38.420
I've gotta let them bunnies 
know who the real hero is.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:42.060
They got Patrick! Please 
hurry to the Godinion!

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:43.740
That's your job.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:46.650
Let me handle things 
here. You get goin'!

00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:48.200
But my unit-

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:50.620
Don't give me that 
bullshit! I said to go!

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:58.460
Outta ammo, huh?

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:04.990
It turned on!

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:05.720
Go!

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:07.120
Sorry!

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:17.670
Randy!

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:22.560
The lives of everyone on Earth are 
hangin' on that information...

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.110
It's cool; just go...

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:26.010
Randy!

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:30.990
Oh, yeah. Please pick up that 
new video I ordered, Chandra...

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:34.190
Randy!

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:39.360
What the hell?

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.760
You're a bummer clear up to the end...

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:46.910
What's the situation?

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:48.830
Black 6 has taken off.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:51.330
I've identified a large explosion 
in our target direction.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:52.410
What does that mean?

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:54.130
There is an enemy battleship!

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:55.420
Offer support fire!

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:56.430
It's too far away!

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:59.590
Please link my unit to 
the fire control system!

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.030
I will calculate the trajectory.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:02.900
Authorization granted!

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.680
Sensors, linked! Coordinate 
axis, transferred!

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:09.720
Roger!

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:11.890
Correcting precision error of 0.3.

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:14.250
Firing all scatter lasers!

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:18.610
There are signs of impact.

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:20.470
I have an 87.5% estimate 
of the targets' location,

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:21.880
speed and projected routes.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:22.780
I'm sending the specifics.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:25.120
I've got the info!

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:27.260
We have a 250% rate of convergence!

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:29.230
Target: The Wulgaru flagship!

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:30.810
My main cannon is ready to fire!

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:31.720
Fire!

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:33.230
I'm firing everything I've got!

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:46.930
Such tactics lack any form of beauty.

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:50.510
It fails to excite my DNA in the least.

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:08.680
Gate's coordinates... verified...

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:55.990
"Genes of Destiny"
